Q: Why does my DirectorySearcher PageSize set to fewer than the number of AD users still return all users? A: <p>You are misunderstanding what the <code>PageSize</code> property refers to. It refers to the number of <em>pages</em> of records. By default, the value is 1, or one page of records. It does not refer to the <em>number of records</em>.</p>
<p>As you noted in your question, your default <code>DirectorySearcher</code> code returns 2000 records. This means one page of results is 2000 records. So, by setting your <code>PageSize</code> property to 2000, you are saying you expect 2000 * 2000 records, or 4,000,000 records.</p>
<p>In reality, you only have 4,066 records in Active Directory, so for you <code>PageSize = 3</code> would be sufficient to return all 4,066 records, since 4,066 / 2,000 = 2.033 (not 2,033). If you had 4,000 total records, then even <code>PageSize = 2</code> would be sufficient.</p>
<p>This code:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>ds.PageSize = 3;
log.Debug(&quot;PageSize=&quot; + ds.PageSize);
log.Debug(&quot;SizeLimit=&quot; + ds.SizeLimit);
results = ds.FindAll();
log.Debug(&quot;AD count: &quot; + results.Count);
</code></pre>
<p>Should return the same AD Count as your 3rd test:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>PageSize=3
SizeLimit=0
AD Count: 4066
</code></pre>
